Initial Creation Date: 2010.10.27

Product added to build tree: Apache Wink 1.2

Person performing tools isolation and addition to build tree: Kaloyan Kolev

Location the product was retrieved from: https://cs.opensource.ibm.com/frs/?group_id=3532

From release V1.0.1.0_20101026 I downloaded the Managed_StandAlone_com.ibm.websphere.jaxrs_1.0.1.1.zip file.

Any special instruction needed to get the product.  Like a special
user name or password. (May not be applicable):

N/A.

Instruction on how you created the tools isolation for this product.
Please include platform you installed on, where you installed it, what
you copied where, etc.:

Downloaded the Managed_StandAlone_com.ibm.websphere.jaxrs_1.0.1.1.zip to D:\temp on my Windows box. 
Extracted the file to the current directory.
Copied the following files from the 'lib/jaxrs_1.X' folder to adks/apache/wink/1.2 folder and checked it into cmvc:
  ibm-wink-jaxrs.jar


Using Eclipse I checked out the SVN wink-jackson-provider source located at:

https://svn.cs.opensource.ibm.com/svn/ibmjaxrs/trunk/wink/wink-providers/wink-jackson-provider

Build the cloasses within it against the ibm-wink-jaxrs.jar and the jaxrs-api.
The build classes I copied into the ibmdi-wink-jaxrs.jar and made sure the directory structure
representing the packages of the classes was not violated.

Then I edited the file META-INF/core/wink-providers and made sure that all the JSON4J providers (currently 3) 
are either removed or commented out. I added the wink provider above the jaxb-xml ones as one line like:

org.apache.wink.providers.jackson.WinkJacksonJaxbJsonProvider

Update History (Use only if you have to actually make more changes after the product
has been used in a tools tree build.  Should be rare) :
-----------------
2010.10.27 - Initial check-in.

-----
Update: Aug 2023

A recent vulnerability scan shows that the version of Apache wink which was 
included in the ibm-wink-jaxrs.jar file contained a vulnerability: 
CVE-2010-2245.

In order to fix this the version of Apache wink was upgraded to 1.4.  In order
to do this:
        1. The contents of the existing jar file was extracted;
        2. The org/apache directory was removed, and then replaced with the
           contents of the org/apache directory from the following jar files:
                wink-client-1.4.jar
                wink-common-1.4.jar
                wink-jackson-provider-1.4.jar
                wink-server-1.4.jar
        3. The ibm-wink-jaxrs.jar jar file was then recreated from the 
           extracted and updated files.

NB: As a part of this update we also need to update the jackson API to a more
    recent version (e.g. 1.9.13).

In addition to this, one of the updates to the Java Bean naming scheme means
that java.util.List field names now default to the plural value of the attribute
name (e.g. the field name for: 'protected List<AtomEntry> entry' used to be
'entry', but is now 'entries').  Our JavaScript has been coded to expect the
singular form of the field name.

To overcome this problem, the Wink source code was downloaded and then the
WinkJacksonJaxbJsonProvider.java class was updated to include a custom
naming schema which removes the plural from java.util.List field names.  The
source code for the updated Java class is contained in the 'src' sub-directory.
The Wink source code was downloaded from:
    https://wink.incubator.apache.org/downloads.html


